module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_last_use_argument_is_cloned_into_a_by_value_parameter

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode, RungRead, FoundOnRung, BelowCeiling }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, MechanicallyPreventable }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data a_last_use_argument_is_cloned_into_a_by_value_parameter: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_last_use_argument_is_cloned_into_a_by_value_parameter" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
      ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "a REQUIRED control that times an emitted accumulator fold (list_map over list_push) against host and goes red outside a constant band, SUFFICIENT FOR a revert of v1.compiler.ownership moved_at_its_only_argument to turn v2-bootstrap red; //gunbc/instruments:member-home-cost case map is that control everywhere except that it is not on the required path."
    }
  },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: the emitted Rust clones a binding at its last use when that use is an argument to a by-value parameter: `v1_rt::rc_list_push(xs.clone(), item.clone())` in std.algebra list_push, and `|acc, item| list_push(acc.clone(), ..)` in a step passed to fold_list. The clone leaves the Rc's strong count at 2 when the callee's make_mut runs, so an im Vector push copies the tail chunk it would otherwise have mutated in place.",
    "HARM: every accumulator built by pushing (list_map, list_flat_map, the list_sort_by_key merge, and any fold whose step pushes) pays a chunk copy per element. The walk stays linear, so no cost-shape gate sees it, but member-home-cost read map at 6.3x host and sort_by at 21.7x, which is the N7 member-home wall.",
    "CAUSE, THE EARLIEST UNJUSTIFIED BOUNDARY: v1.compiler.ownership walk_expr classified only a tail position as Consumed and every other use as Read, which the module's own note calls the never-classified residue. build_movable_set admits a binding only with zero Read edges, so no argument was ever moved. The clone at each site is downstream of that one classification. Repairing a site (eliding the closure's clone, or list_push's) changes nothing alone: measured, one elided clone left 16000 of 16000 pushes shared.",
    "PROTOTYPE READING (a one-off, not an instrument): the emitted list_map shape hand-transcribed with v1_rt::rc_list_push instrumented to count Rc strong_count above 1 at make_mut, remote amd64, 2026-10-24, im 15.1.0, n = 2000 to 64000, best of 7, outputs equal to host at every n. As emitted: every push shared, 9.1x host. With only the closure's clone elided: every push shared, 9.1x. With both last-use clones moved: no push shared, 1.43x host.",
    "THE REPAIR: a bare binding passed as an ExprCall argument records a PassedByValue edge (v1.compiler.ownership walk_call_argument), and a binding whose only edge is PassedByValue is movable (moved_at_its_only_argument). It is not Consumed, because semantic_consumer_count keys SharedError and an OwnershipViolation. A lambda bound to a declared callee's parameter gets its own proof over its own parameters (v1.compiler.emit_rust user_call_lambda_emit_info), because the function's proof records every name in a lambda body as a capture. Method receivers stay Read: their lowering templates are not audited for splicing the receiver once, which is the open frontier.",
    "A NEW EDGE KIND MUST BE COUNTED BY EVERY RULE THAT COUNTED THE ONE IT REPLACES. The first regen round with only the new arm emitted v1.compiler.ownership fold_terminal_expr as a move of `body` into let_body followed by `body` returned on the Absent arm, and the seed refused to build (rustc E0382, use of moved value `body`). The pre-existing tail-consume arm admits a binding when whole_value_borrow_count is zero, and that count read Read and Threaded only; the argument had been a Read and now was not. whole_value_borrow_count counts PassedByValue, and max_usage_by_fan_out carries the other path's PassedByValue edges as it carries its Reads, so a path that moves and then consumes cannot pass for a single consume.",
    "THE CALLEE IS A USE. The second round built the ownership mirror and then refused std.algebra: fold_list_right as `snoc(fold_list_right(t, empty, snoc), h)` (rustc E0505, cannot move out of `snoc` because it is borrowed) and zip_map as `zip_map(ta, tb, f)` then `f(ha, hb)` (E0382). walk_expr never recorded the callee of a call, so each binding showed one edge, the argument, and was moved into it while still being called. The callee now records an Invoked edge, a whole-value use that blocks a move and stays out of binding_fan_out so a parameter that is only called does not become read-only.",
    "EXECUTED, 2026-10-24, remote amd64, one dispatch per arm, main plus the member-home-cost control (gunbc.instruments.member_home_cost_native, with list_map as fold_list plus list_push). BEFORE: map at 16000 is 1596456 ns against 254802 host, 6.27x, not_held at every n. AFTER, with the regen round's candidates for the whole stage0 corpus installed into the seed (98 files, the seed built from them, which is the compile proof that the rule emits no use of a moved value anywhere in that corpus): map at 16000 is 247660 ns against 200870 host, 1.23x, held at every n; every case agreed with host. In the regenerated corpus std.algebra list_push emits `v1_rt::rc_list_push(xs, item)` and the list_map step `v1_rt::rc_list_push(acc, f(item))`; list_sort_by_key keeps `xs.clone()` at both of its uses (list_map, then length) and moves `order`, its one use. sort_by stayed at 19.2x: its remaining cost is not this class but the merge walk, which is not a cursor walk because it passes a list back unchanged and appends it at the exit, so every step pays an Rc'd skip on both lists.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.ownership", decl_name: "walk_call_argument"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.ownership", decl_name: "moved_at_its_only_argument"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.ownership", decl_name: "build_movable_set"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.emit_rust", decl_name: "user_call_lambda_emit_info"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "std.algebra", decl_name: "list_push"),
  ],
}
